// Edit — Change a draft's lines, customer or description.
//
// Changes what a DRAFT bills, as « Modifier » in the web app: its lines (the whole list: add, change, remove and
// reorder them in one write), its customer, its description; an absent member is unchanged. Only while the draft
// has not left the organization — not mailed, shared by a link, read online, sent to the e-invoicing network, paid
// (GET …/editability says; 409 billing.invoice.not-editable otherwise). The write replays the creation: the price
// customization guard (a line kept as it was keeps its price), the tenant and tag scope guards, the totals
// recomputed, and a new customer's recipient, legal details and discount. A validated invoice is never changed
// (409): it is corrected by a credit note. A draft whose lines take from a stock (chosen with a stock lot in the
// web app) keeps its lines and customer there (409, reason STOCK_TRACKED); one made from delivery forms keeps its
// lines, linked to them, and its customer, whose forms they bill (409, reason DELIVERY_FORMS); its description
// still changes. A body that changes nothing writes nothing. Its tags: PATCH …/{invoiceId}. With If-Match, refused
// (412) if the invoice changed since it was read. Send an Idempotency-Key to retry safely.
