// Debit — Debit an invoice by SEPA.
//
// Starts the SEPA debit of what remains due on an invoice the caller can see, through its customer's mandate, as
// from the web app: the invoice moves to SEPA_PENDING (a VALIDATED one is shared first), the customer is told, and
// the payment appears in the invoice's payments once Stripe settled the debit (a few business days; SEPA_FAILED if
// the bank rejects it). Refused before anything moves: a demo organization, the collection off or paused, a plan
// without SEPA debits, no account, an account Stripe suspended, a status that takes no debit (a debit in progress
// included), no mandate, an amount outside the bounds, a quota reached. A session passes the passkey step-up
// stripe.collect (bound to the invoice); an API key holding the right needs none. Send an Idempotency-Key to retry
// safely: a retry never debits twice (the second meets SEPA_PENDING).
